+   "text": "Good morning Lakshmi garu, thank you for bringing Ravi today. I will ask some questions while he plays, is that okay? Yes madam, avunu, that is fine. He already went to the toy corner. When you talk to Ravi at home, does he look at you? No madam, he does not look at us when we talk. Even when I feed him he never looks in my eyes. And when you call his name from another room? He does not turn when we call his name. I call Ravi, Ravi, many times, kani he keeps playing. Note: child did not respond to name in three attempts, rate item 5 as 4. Same thing at home, madam. My mother says he is in his own world. Let us talk about speech. Did Ravi ever say words? Yes, at age 2 he said a few words, amma, nanna, ball. Then slowly he stopped talking. Now he says no words at all. Thank you for telling me, that is important. Did anything else happen around that time? Nothing special. My husband said boys talk late, so we waited. Kani the words did not come back. How does he play at home? He lines up his toys in one long line, cars, blocks, even spoons. He plays alone, he does not play with his cousins. Does he keep any one toy with him all the time? Yes, one small red car. He takes it to bed, to the bathroom, everywhere. Does he make other sounds or repeat things he hears? He repeats lines from cartoons, the same line again and again, but not to talk to us. Does he point at things he wants, or to show you something? No, he does not point. If he wants water he pulls my hand to the kitchen. How does he react to noises at home? He covers his ears at the mixer and the pressure cooker whistle. Sometimes he runs and hides behind the sofa. And when he is happy or excited? He flaps his hands very fast and jumps on his toes, chala fast, when the cartoon song comes. Note: child flapped hands twice during play today, rate item 24 as 4. Yes, just now also he did it with the red car. What happens when something changes in his routine? Big tantrum. One day we changed the route to school because of traffic. He screamed and kicked for half an hour. When he is upset like that, does he ever hurt himself? Yes madam, this worries me most. He hits his own head with his hand when he is upset. I hold his hands so he is safe. Thank you, that helps me. Does he come to tell you about his day? No, he never comes to tell us anything. He only takes my hand when he needs something. How are his sleep and food? Sleep is okay but late. He eats only rice and curd from the same plate every day. Thank you Lakshmi garu. I only document what I see and what you share, and we will plan the next steps together. Thank you madam, chala thanks. I just want to help him.",
